# Tell GitHub Linguist to ignore vendored W3C test fixtures.
# These are third-party test data files (not RDF.jl source code) and should
# not influence the repository's detected language breakdown.
test/w3c/fixtures/** linguist-vendored -text

# -text: never translate line endings in the vendored fixtures. They are
# third-party conformance data and must be checked out byte-for-byte as
# published. Several expected-result files carry literal newlines inside
# literal values — the SPARQL 1.0 regex tests for the s, m and x options among
# them — so a CRLF checkout on Windows silently changes what they assert.
